Z||000000||Phil||09-15-1999||11:11 AM||||I have a 97 Buick and computer in my 88 Formula with a 5sp. The computer thinks the trans is slipping because sometimes my rpm's exceed the set parameters for my speed therefore I always have a CHECK ENGINE light. I removed the bulb but an auto electric shop said that by doing that I put my computer into a reduced power mode. Does any one know if this is true or not? Just to be safe I plan on putting a 22 ohm resistor in the bulb socket, but I would like to know if this is really nessesary?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-15-1999||11:41 AM||||First time I ever heared that and although it might be true for other cars, I'm pretty sure it's not true for the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-15-1999||12:47 PM||||one of 2 things is wrong. DO NOT put a resistor in the socket. fix it and put the bulb back in. Coulde be either or both of the below.<P>1. the ECM has the wrong prom for your application. replace the prom with one for that motor and a 5 speed. you can find these in slavage yards. make sure the 2 ECMs are the same. ECM proms can only be moved between the same type ECM.<P>2. the clutch is probably slipping some. replace it, preferably with a centerforce kit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||09-15-1999||05:33 PM||||My motor is a  97 S/C 3800 and was not available with a manual- ergo no compatable PCM. I have no clutch slippage but evidently when I run it up in the lower gears my RPMs read higher that the computer thinks it should for the speed info it is recieving. (5400 RPM for 40 MPH) just guessing on those numbers. The error code is somthing about vss input. Nobody wants to reprogram my PCM to have it ignore that error that's why the bulb removal or else live with the light eternally on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||09-16-1999||06:52 PM||||What is the error? I'll bet it's a code 39/740 equivalent (TCC excess slip).<P>That's the problem with the new PCM's. Change the code is a bear. It's a 4T65E trans too, right?<P>The bulb being dead will likely set a Quad Driver failure, but not cause the ECM to shutdown.<P>The lack of TCC and other things due to the slip code would be more of a worry.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-16-1999||07:55 PM||||you sure that none of the chip makers has code for that system? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||09-17-1999||02:02 AM||||There are a couple of places that reprogram the PCM (it's flash), but I've heard various horror stories on it. The 96 and up PCM code is quite different from the 95 and below.<P>I just finished helping a guy get his 97 Series II SC engine running on a 92 ECM using a 4T60E. We had to swap to the digital EGR. The 94-95 ECM's from Series I engines is great for running 96 and up Series II engines. They just can't control the 4T65E, so we used a 4T60E. Very nice and easy to increase the power. The 4T60E is quite capable of handling the Series II's power.<P>Funny, the 92-93 ECM from the Series I supercharged engines has everything to handle the 125C or 440 on top of the 4T60E.<P>That's why I considering a swap into my 86 Fiero. If I can get a 4T60E, I will use the 125C. How long will it last.Beats me!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||09-17-1999||02:05 AM||||I was thinking, you could switch to the 92-93 ECM from a Bonne SSEi, switch to the 125C code and digital EGR and have a functioning system. Some decel enleanment changes would be needed, but it would work pretty dang good.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||09-17-1999||12:29 PM||||Actually the thing runs fine, goes quite well and everything seems to work(7000 mi so far). It's just annoying to have the CHECK ENGINE light on all the time that is why I removed the bulb.BTW I have the standard Getrag 5sp with a modified speed sensor. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||09-17-1999||12:53 PM||||Hey, if it ain't broke, don't fix it!<P>The error codes are likely TCC slip and possibly Quad A/B driver errors unless they added resistors to the shift and TCC solenoid outputs. Since a failure in these sections cause a forced third gear, about the worse thing I would expect is that it is running in limited torque for third. Might be some SC bypassing. Still ought to run pretty good. <P>||||reg||1
